## Location
`rust/lichen-oscore/src/lib.rs:1227` — `decrypt_response_in_place()`, the inner body parsing.

## Problem
The request decryption path (`decrypt_request_in_place` at line 901) was upgraded to use `parse_inner_body()` which returns `Err(OscoreError::InvalidParam)` on malformed option body (truncated extended delta/length bytes, invalid encodings). The response decryption path still uses `find_payload_marker()` which returns `Option<usize>` — and its `None` case at line 1229 maps to `(rest, &[][..])`, silently treating all remaining data as options even when the option body is truncated/malformed.

```rust
// Response path (line 1227) — uses find_payload_marker, no validation:
let (options_slice, payload_slice) = match find_payload_marker(rest) {
    Some(pos) => (&rest[..pos], &rest[pos + 1..]),
    None => (rest, &[][..]),  // silent fallthrough on malformed input
};

// Request path (line 901) — uses parse_inner_body, validates:
let (options_slice, payload_slice) = parse_inner_body(rest)?;
// Returns Err(OscoreError::InvalidParam) on malformed input
```

## Impact
- Malformed response with truncated CoAP option body bypasses validation
- Inconsistent parsing between request and response paths
- `find_payload_marker` returns `None` on: truncated length bytes, delta=15 w/o payload marker, length=15 w/o delta=15 — all silently treated as "all options, no payload"

## Fix
Replace `find_payload_marker` usage at line 1227 with `parse_inner_body` for consistency with the request path. The response code at line 1219 already validates `code >> 5` in `2..=5` (CoAP response classes), so the parsing mismatch is the only gap.
